      "content": "The 1st, 2nd and 3rd ionisation enthalpies, I<sub>1</sub>, I<sub>2</sub> and I<sub>3</sub>, of four atoms with atomic numbers n, n + 1, n + 2, and n + 3, where n &lt; 10, are tabulated below. What is the value of n?<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2020 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Periodic Table &amp; Periodicity Question 2 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lf44lr1c/8eeb9789-06ff-4cce-a14a-f8cd59a36589/00a22200-c022-11ed-b552-e7a88d45dbe9/file-1lf44lr1d.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">",
